      "writtenOn": "2024-09-09T18:39:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Remember, you only need to issue a disconnect call to native if the message that got us here was a user driven `DISCONNECT` message. If it was a stack event carrying a DISCONNECTED state, then we can pass on through to Disconnected.\n\nOtherwise, as this stands, all incoming disconnections will yield timeouts.\n\ni.e.:\n```\nif (getCurrentMessage().what \u003d\u003d DISCONNECT) {\n    debug(\"Disconnecting: issue disconnect call to native\");\n    if (!mNativeInterface.disconnect(dev)) {\n        error(\"Disconnecting: disconnectNative failed for \" + dev);\n    }\n    sendMessageDelayed(DISCONNECTING_TIMEOUT, DISCONNECTING_TIMEOUT_MS);\n} else {\n    transitionTo(mDisconnected);\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2000,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2000,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "73f16ac1cc8d25f44e7cfa52c279145b9bae2a92",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
